WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.937
Time series pre-training promises to cut labeling
costs and boost many downstream tasks,

00:00:06.017 --> 00:00:10.722
but the standard recipes borrowed from vision and
language fall short.

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:16.739
Randomly masking a series or computing series-wise
similarity tends to distort or ignore

00:00:16.819 --> 00:00:20.773
the temporal correlations that make time series
meaningful.

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:22.892
This paper introduces TimeSiam,

00:00:22.972 --> 00:00:28.020
a simple but effective self-supervised framework
built on Siamese networks.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:30.208
Instead of masking in isolation,

00:00:30.288 --> 00:00:36.292
TimeSiam samples a past and a current subseries
from the same sequence and trains Siamese

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:40.942
encoders to reconstruct the masked current series
from the past one,

00:00:41.022 --> 00:00:44.975
explicitly modeling how observations correlate
across time.

00:00:45.055 --> 00:00:51.949
Learnable lineage embeddings let a single model
capture correlations at many different time distances.

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:57.692
Across thirteen benchmarks and two mainstream
tasks, forecasting and classification,

00:00:57.772 --> 00:01:03.230
TimeSiam sets a new state of the art in both
in-domain and cross-domain settings.
